<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kabasa</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kabasa was the royal capital of the Kingdom of Ndongo in present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/angola">Angola</a>, on the plateau between the Lukala and Kwanza rivers. A Portuguese embassy under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paulo-dias-de-novais">Paulo Dias de Novais</a> reached it in 1560. Portuguese forces and their allies attacked it repeatedly in the early 17th century, and Ndongo's rulers later moved their base east towards Matamba.</p></div>
